                <pb facs="0373" n="293" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg293"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.154/257: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-19T12:00:00-06:00">October 19,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 10:52 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>102. Department’s telegram No. 61, October 11, 4 p.m. Minister of Fomento states
                    agreeable if engineers come about November 1st but not later, during rainy
                    season.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
